-- title:
--   Modular unit Δ(q)/Δ(qᵖ) at the Gauss prime
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to the $L$-subfield generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map $L((q)) \leftarrow \mathbb{Q}((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\,\mathrm{jNumQ}(q)$, and let $\mathcal{O} = \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$. Let $u, u' \in \mathcal{O}$ have $q$-expansions the image of $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$, respectively $p^{12}$ times the inverse of that image, where $\Delta(q) = q\cdot(\text{the }\eta\text{-unit power series})$ and $\Delta(q^p)$ is its $q \mapsto q^p$ substitution. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ characterised by: $f \in W_0$ iff there are $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$; and let $P_0 \subseteq \mathcal{O}$ be an ideal characterised by $b \in P_0$ iff $b$ is a non-unit of $W_0$. Then $u \notin P_0$, $u' \in P_0$, and for every monic $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ of positive degree one has $g(u) \notin P_0$.
--
--   On the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the local ring $A$ of $\mathbb{Z}[\zeta_p]$ above $p$, this records the behaviour of the modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ at the prime cut out by the Gauss valuation: it is a unit there, its companion $p^{12}/u$ lies in the prime, and its reduction satisfies no monic integral equation, i.e. is transcendental over the residue field. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval_chartAlgFin_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval_chartAlgFin_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
